# Inferenza su premesse nello stesso turno, KB completa. Le lezioni qui sono
# input del test della meccanica, NON training fattuale da persistere.
# La regola sul pericolo e' un'ipotesi didattica sufficiente: l'antecedente
# escluso non autorizza la negazione della conclusione (negazione antecedente).
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test lessons are received in natural language]
> scorpions are venomous
<~ Learned rule: venomous(X) :- scorpion(X).
> bees are venomous
<~ Learned rule:
> wasps are venomous
<~ Learned rule:
> vipers are venomous
<~ Learned rule:
> mosquitoes are not venomous
<~ no mosquito is venomous
> dogs are not venomous
<~ no dog is venomous
> if someone is stung by something venomous then they are in danger
<~ Learned: whoever is stung by something venomous is endangered.
> if someone is bitten by something venomous then they are in danger
<~ Learned: whoever is bitten by something venomous is endangered.

[test ellipsis binds the relation and preserves both people]
> Marco was stung by a scorpion and Luca by a mosquito: which of the two is in danger?
<~ Marco is in danger: Marco was stung by a scorpion, which is venomous.
<~ Luca was stung by a mosquito, which is not venomous.
<~ This rule does not establish whether Luca is in danger.
<! Luca is not in danger
!query! stung_by(marco, scorpion_of_marco)
!query! scorpion(scorpion_of_marco)
!query! mosquito(mosquito_of_luca)
!query! holds1(endangered, marco)

[test exchanged roles]
> Luca was stung by a scorpion and Marco by a mosquito: which of the two is in danger?
<~ Luca is in danger:
<~ This rule does not establish whether Marco is in danger.
<! Marco is not in danger

[test two supported conclusions]
> Anna was stung by a bee and Sara by a wasp: which of the two is in danger?
<~ Anna is in danger:
<~ Sara is in danger:

[test two excluded antecedents do not prove either conclusion false]
> Anna was stung by a mosquito and Sara by a mosquito: which of the two is in danger?
<~ This rule does not establish whether Anna is in danger.
<~ This rule does not establish whether Sara is in danger.
<! is not in danger

[test an unknown kind is not a negative fact]
> Marco was stung by a scorpion and Luca by a jellyfish: which of the two is in danger?
<~ Marco is in danger:
<~ I can't tell whether Luca is in danger:
<! Luca is not in danger

[test another relation uses the same reading and inference]
> Paolo was bitten by a viper and Carlo by a dog: which of the two is in danger?
<~ Paolo is in danger: Paolo was bitten by a viper, which is venomous.
<~ Carlo was bitten by a dog, which is not venomous.
<! Carlo is not in danger

[test two full premises and a mixed relation]
> Marco was stung by a scorpion and Luca was bitten by a viper: which of the two is in danger?
<~ Marco is in danger:
<~ Luca is in danger: Luca was bitten by a viper

[test singular question]
> Marco was stung by a scorpion: is Marco in danger?
<~ Marco is in danger:

[test restriction retract and spoken reteach]
!forget exists_restriction(endangered, stung_by, venomous)
> Marco was stung by a scorpion: is Marco in danger?
<! Marco is in danger:
> if someone is stung by something venomous then they are in danger
<~ Learned:
> Marco was stung by a scorpion: is Marco in danger?
<~ Marco is in danger:

[test new surface grows and retracts without rebuilding]
> Marco was pricked by a scorpion: is Marco in danger?
<! Marco is in danger:
!assert relation_surface(stung_by, "was pricked by")
> Marco was pricked by a scorpion: is Marco in danger?
<~ Marco is in danger: Marco was pricked by a scorpion
!forget relation_surface(stung_by, "was pricked by")
> Marco was pricked by a scorpion: is Marco in danger?
<! Marco is in danger:

[test existing knowledge survives hypothetical cleanup]
!assert scorpion(scorpion_of_marco)
!assert stung_by(marco, scorpion_of_marco)
> Marco was stung by a scorpion and Luca by a mosquito: which of the two is in danger?
<~ Marco is in danger:
!query scorpion(scorpion_of_marco)
!query stung_by(marco, scorpion_of_marco)
!query! mosquito(mosquito_of_luca)
!forget scorpion(scorpion_of_marco)
!forget stung_by(marco, scorpion_of_marco)

[test translations are taught]
> the italian for scorpion is scorpione
<~ scorpione
> the italian for mosquito is zanzara
<~ zanzara
# Questa traduzione e quella di dog sono gia' nella KB viva.
!query tr(bee, ape)
> the italian for wasp is vespa
<~ vespa
> the italian for viper is vipera
<~ vipera
!query tr(dog, cane)
> the italian for venomous is velenoso
<~ velenoso

[test italian ellipsis and feminine agreement]
> Marco è stato punto da uno scorpione e Luca da una zanzara: chi dei due è in pericolo?
<~ Marco è in pericolo:
<~ Luca: è stato punto da una zanzara, che non è velenosa.
<~ Questa regola non basta a decidere se è in pericolo.
<! Luca no:
!query! stung_by(marco, scorpion_of_marco)
!query! scorpion(scorpion_of_marco)

[test italian all positive]
> Anna è stata punta da un'ape e Sara da una vespa: chi dei due è in pericolo?
<~ Anna è in pericolo:
<~ Sara è in pericolo:

[test italian bite with a full second premise]
> Paolo è stato morso da una vipera e Carlo è stato morso da un cane: chi dei due è in pericolo?
<~ Paolo è in pericolo:
<~ Carlo: è stato morso da un cane, che non è velenoso.

[test italian unknown is not no]
> Marco è stato punto da uno scorpione e Luca da una medusa: chi dei due è in pericolo?
<~ Marco è in pericolo:
<~ Di Luca non posso dirlo:
<! Luca no:

[test ordinary question still uses the real world]
> what is the capital of france
< Paris.
